{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgHa3xDeo1VgyKTJNcey3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"For July 2025, departures from SFO, by reporting carrier:\n\n| Carrier | Scheduled departures | Cancelled | Departures counted | Avg departure delay (min) | Share delayed >15 min |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| United (UA) | 5,112 | 56 | 5,056 | 15.6 | 21.3% |\n| Alaska (AS) | 1,041 | 22 | 1,019 | 13.7 | 22.0% |\n| Delta (DL) | 1,233 | 9 | 1,224 | 17.2 | 24.3% |\n| Southwest (WN) | 704 | 5 | 699 | 22.8 | 39.6% |\n\n**Where the numbers came from**\n- **File:** the BTS \"Reporting Carrier On-Time Performance (1987–present)\" monthly file for July 2025. I downloaded it directly from `https://transtats.bts.gov/PREZIP/On_Time_Reporting_Carrier_On_Time_Performance_1987_present_2025_7.zip`. It is the raw DOT/BTS data behind the TranStats \"On-Time Performance\" tables.\n- **Filter:** `Origin = SFO`, grouped by `Reporting_Airline` (UA, AS, DL, WN).\n- **Average delay:** the mean of `DepDelayMinutes` across flights that actually departed. BTS sets early departures to 0 in this field. The plain signed `DepDelay` average, which lets early departures offset late ones, is lower: UA 12.7, AS 10.6, DL 14.0, WN 21.8.\n- **Share delayed >15 min:** the mean of `DepDel15`, which BTS flags when a flight departs 15 or more minutes after its scheduled time. Strictly, that means at least 15 minutes, not more than 15.\n- **Cancelled flights:** I excluded them from both measures. BTS leaves their delay fields blank.\n\n**Caveats for the slide**\n- **Mainline carriers only:** these figures cover each carrier's own flights. Regional flights sold as United Express or Alaska are filed under the operating airline, such as SkyWest (OO), so they aren't in the United or Alaska rows. SkyWest alone had 2,951 SFO departures in July.\n- **Rows are not airline-wide SFO totals:** the Alaska and Delta rows rest on about 1,000 to 1,200 departures each. That is much smaller than United's 5,000.\n- **Possible revisions:** the file I downloaded is dated 14 Oct 2025. BTS can revise monthly files, so recheck it if the slide needs to match a later release."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":853,"cache_read_input_tokens":20831,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":853},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"42275393-6fae-489b-a686-1c10bd6962d7","uuid":"cbec60b0-85c0-4c9f-9588-9dd9ca19e195","timestamp":"2026-10-22T16:12:55.739Z","request_id":"req_011CgHa3wsJsrXzn2UWjGBdx"}
